        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: stereotype content model, warmth, competence\n- People: Susan Fiske, Amy Cuddy, Peter Glick, Jun Xu\n- Roles: social psychologists, author, lecturer\n\nFacts:\n- The stereotype content model is a psychological theory that hypothesizes that stereotypes have two dimensions: warmth and competence.\n- The stereotype content model was first proposed by social psychologist Susan Fiske and her colleagues Amy Cuddy, Peter Glick, and Jun Xu.\n- Amy Joy Casselberry Cuddy, born in 1972, is an American social psychologist, author, and lecturer.\n- Amy Cuddy is known for research on stereotyping and discrimination, emotions, power, nonverbal behavior, and the effects of social stimuli on hormone levels.",
